{"id":32240,"title":"A survey on participating media rendering techniques","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00371-005-0287-1","final_url":"https://inria.hal.science/inria-00510151/document","year":2005,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":"10.1007/s00371-005-0287-1","arxiv":null,"sha256":"e50dd0f2f853c3f6402ebaaed8ca30cdd4d118433c32f28b5286b52648edb953","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793061657.843214,"text_chars":128252,"abstract":"International audienceRendering participating media is important for a number of domains, ranging from commercial applications (entertainment, virtual reality) to simulation systems (driving, ﬂying and space simulators) and safety analyses (driving conditions, sign visibility). This article surveys global illumination algorithms for environments including participating media. It reviews both appearance-based and physically-based media methods, including the single scattering and the more general multiple-scattering techniques. The objective of the survey is the characterization of all these methods: Identiﬁcation of their base techniques, assumptions, limitations and range of utilization. We conclude with some reﬂections about the suitability of the methods depending on the speciﬁc application involved, and possible future research lines","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://inria.hal.science/inria-00510151/document","https://doi.org/10.1007/s00371-005-0287-1","https://inria.hal.science/inria-00510151","https://core.ac.uk/works/13818840","https://inria.hal.science/inria-00510151v1"],"cited_by":[{"path":"1080-frustum-corner-ray-reconstruction.md","name":"Frustum Corner Ray Reconstruction","k":5},{"path":"1891-spherical-camera-control.md","name":"Spherical Camera Control","k":1},{"path":"1080-standard-constant-step-ray-marching.md","name":"Standard Constant Step Ray Marching","k":5},{"path":"1395-p-n-method-spherical-harmonics.md","name":"P-N Method (Spherical Harmonics)","k":2},{"path":"1297-psf-based-multiple-scattering-rendering.md","name":"PSF-based Multiple Scattering Rendering","k":1},{"path":"2372-diffusion-approximation.md","name":"Diffusion Approximation","k":2},{"path":"1891-zonal-method.md","name":"Zonal Method","k":1},{"path":"3289-single-scattering-atmosphere-rendering.md","name":"Single-Scattering Atmosphere Rendering","k":8},{"path":"5340-single-scattering-approximations.md","name":"Single Scattering Approximations","k":1},{"path":"4976-photon-beam-methods.md","name":"Photon Beam Methods","k":1},{"path":"5620-photon-based-methods.md","name":"Photon-based Methods","k":2},{"path":"6666-bidirectional-path-tracing.md","name":"Bidirectional Path Tracing","k":2},{"path":"8722-metropolis-light-transport-for-participating-media.md","name":"Metropolis Light Transport for Participating Media","k":1},{"path":"8682-volume-rendering-integral.md","name":"Volume Rendering Integral","k":2},{"path":"11373-optimized-ray-casting.md","name":"Optimized Ray Casting","k":2},{"path":"5547-photon-mapping-for-participating-media.md","name":"Photon Mapping for Participating Media","k":1},{"path":"9399-spectral-scattering-model-for-atmosphere.md","name":"Spectral Scattering Model for Atmosphere","k":1},{"path":"10687-multiple-scattering-models.md","name":"Multiple Scattering Models","k":1},{"path":"9013-optimized-monte-carlo-integrator.md","name":"Optimized Monte Carlo Integrator","k":1},{"path":"12248-premoze-et-al-path-integration.md","name":"Premoze et al. Path Integration","k":1},{"path":"12250-constant-distance-sampling.md","name":"Constant Distance Sampling","k":1},{"path":"12221-zonal-method-bhate-and-tokuta.md","name":"Zonal Method (Bhate and Tokuta)","k":1},{"path":"7874-photon-beam-mapping.md","name":"Photon Beam Mapping","k":4},{"path":"12347-fake-media-methods.md","name":"Fake Media Methods","k":1},{"path":"12251-klassen-s-spectral-atmospheric-method.md","name":"Klassen's Spectral Atmospheric Method","k":1},{"path":"12300-progressive-refinement-zonal-method.md","name":"P